{"id":"3a499bbcd4da13c648eebe0ef489afbb6bca69a5","axis":"silent","repo":"datafuselabs/databend","sha":"3a499bbcd4da13c648eebe0ef489afbb6bca69a5","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"Cargo.lock","lines":["@@ -5799,6 +5799,7 @@ dependencies = [","  \"goldenfile\",","  \"headers\",","  \"hex\",","+ \"hmac 0.12.1\",","  \"http 1.3.1\",","  \"humantime\",","  \"hyper-util\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/designs/http-query-token.md","lines":["@@ -97,6 +97,46 @@ has already committed and is not a signal to automatically re-execute it.","   while a well-formed query-token request without retained query state gives 404."," - Duplicate `X-DATABEND-AUTH-METHOD` headers are rejected on authenticated endpoints."," ","+## Credential binding for existing clients","+","+Clients that do not use query tokens get query-scoped access from a credential","+binding. On submission with a password, JWT or key-pair credential, the server","+stores an HMAC (per-process random key) of the requested tenant,","+`X-DATABEND-AUTH-METHOD` and the exact `Authorization` header in the query record;","+the credential itself is not retained. Native session tokens are not bound: they","+are cheap to verify and must keep honoring explicit logout.","+","+If a user-level or applicable global network policy applies at submission, the","+binding also records the effective client IPv4 address used by ordinary","+authentication. It matches only follow-ups from that same address; a missing,","+invalid or different address does not match. A policy-bound submission without a","+usable address cannot establish a binding. When no policy applies at submission,","+the binding does not compare IP addresses.","+","+Network policy is evaluated at submission, not again on a bound follow-up. Changes","+made after submission (including attaching a policy) do not revoke a retained","+binding. New SQL and unbound follow-ups still use ordinary authentication and","+current policy. IP matching relies on the same trusted client-IP source as network","+policy: when forwarding headers are used, a trusted proxy must set them and","+clients must not be able to bypass it.","+","+A state/page/final/kill request without the explicit `query-token` method whose","+binding matches the target query, sent from the query's own client session (or","+without a session if the query has none), is authorized as the query owner without","+user or password-policy lookups in Meta. It is not a login: it is not written to the","+login history, cannot count towards password lockout, and does not renew the client","+session or its temporary tables. Any other credential or session, including a newly","+created one, falls back to ordinary authentication and ownership checks. An explicit","+`query-token` request never falls back: a wrong token is 401 even if `Authorization`","+equals the submission credential.","+","+The submission credential keeps working for its own query after a password change,","+credential expiry or user deletion, but cannot submit new SQL. Credentials that","+change on every request, such as key-pair JWTs, never match and keep the existing","+behavior. Once the query record is gone (expiry, removal or restart) there is","+nothing to match, so a stale credential falls back to ordinary authentication and","+gets 401, whereas a query-token request gets 404 without Meta access.","+"," ## Transport and secrecy"," "," Use TLS. Never put tokens in URLs or unredacted logs/traces. Token-bearing responses"],"additions":40,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/query/service/Cargo.toml","lines":["@@ -139,6 +139,7 @@ geo = { workspace = true }"," geo-index = { workspace = true }"," headers = { workspace = true }"," hex = { workspace = true }","+hmac = { workspace = true }"," http = { workspace = true }"," humantime = { workspace = true }"," itertools = { workspace = true }"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/query/service/src/servers/http/middlewar